{"collection_id":"aggregation-public-explainer","description":"A public-safe guide to Matías Iglesias's governed research notes on aggregation and aggregate volatility. Each card links to the source note that supports it.","items":[{"canonical_url":"https://github.com/matuteiglesias/thesis/blob/7265018750db0f96b69efd4048aedad06ad803fc/docs/Aggregation/chapter1_08.md","contributors":["Matías Iglesias"],"facets":{"explainer_section":"Question"},"item_id":"repo.thesis:aggregation-question","kind":"research-explainer-section","source_ref":{"authority":"repo.thesis","object_id":"docs/Aggregation/chapter1_08.md","url":"https://github.com/matuteiglesias/thesis/blob/7265018750db0f96b69efd4048aedad06ad803fc/docs/Aggregation/chapter1_08.md"},"summary":"Why do aggregate fluctuations remain substantial when many individual shocks might appear to cancel out?","tags":["aggregation","volatility"],"title":"Question"},{"canonical_url":"https://github.com/matuteiglesias/thesis/blob/7265018750db0f96b69efd4048aedad06ad803fc/docs/Aggregation/chapter1_04.md","contributors":["Matías Iglesias"],"facets":{"explainer_section":"Why it matters"},"item_id":"repo.thesis:aggregation-why","kind":"research-explainer-section","source_ref":{"authority":"repo.thesis","object_id":"docs/Aggregation/chapter1_04.md","url":"https://github.com/matuteiglesias/thesis/blob/7265018750db0f96b69efd4048aedad06ad803fc/docs/Aggregation/chapter1_04.md"},"summary":"The research notes frame aggregation as a problem for interpreting macroeconomic volatility from firm-level evidence rather than assuming a representative agent explains all movement.","tags":["macroeconomics","aggregation"],"title":"Why it matters"},{"canonical_url":"https://github.com/matuteiglesias/thesis/blob/7265018750db0f96b69efd4048aedad06ad803fc/docs/Aggregation/chapter1_02.md","contributors":["Matías Iglesias"],"facets":{"explainer_section":"Evidence/data"},"item_id":"repo.thesis:aggregation-evidence","kind":"research-explainer-section","source_ref